    "name": "Sherwin-Williams SuperDeck Exterior Semi-Transparent Stain",
    "amazonUrl": "",
    "bottomLine": "A durable, contractor-favored stain with strong color options for fences that need to look sharp.",
    "pros": [
      "Sold and tinted at Sherwin-Williams stores",
      "Oil and waterborne versions available",
      "Wide color range with custom tinting",
      "Designed for decks, fences and siding",
      "Good support and color matching for touch-ups"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Higher price than big-box brands",
      "Waterborne version needs care to avoid lap marks",
      "Store availability limited to Sherwin-Williams locations"
    ],
    "description": "SuperDeck is Sherwin-Williams' exterior wood stain line, and its semi-transparent version is a common contractor choice for fences, decks and siding. Buying from a paint store has real advantages on a fence project: staff can tint a wide range of colors, match a previous batch for touch-ups and recommend the right sprayer tip. The line includes oil-based and waterborne versions, so you can choose based on your state's VOC rules and your tolerance for drying time. Owners commonly report even color and good longevity on vertical surfaces. The waterborne version dries faster, which shortens the window for overlapping passes, so work in shade and keep a wet edge. The oil version is more forgiving on long runs. It costs more than big-box brands, and you have to buy it at a Sherwin-Williams location, but frequent sales often narrow the gap. For a fence that is a visible part of the house's look, the color control is worth it. Prices were roughly 45 to 70 dollars per gallon at the time of writing."
  },
  {
    "id": "olympic-maximum",
    "badge": "Best Big-Box Value",
