  },
  {
    "id": "behr-premium-solid",
    "badge": "Best for Old Fences",
    "category": "Solid color stain",
    "name": "BEHR Premium Solid Color Waterproofing Stain & Sealer",
    "amazonUrl": "",
    "bottomLine": "The best way to make an old, patched or mismatched fence look uniform again.",
    "pros": [
      "Hides weathering, patches and mismatched boards",
      "Wide color range at Home Depot",
      "Long life on vertical surfaces",
      "Soap-and-water cleanup",
      "Moderate price per gallon"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Hides the wood grain completely",
      "Can peel if applied over old penetrating stain or damp wood",
      "Usually needs two coats"
    ],
    "description": "BEHR Premium Solid Color Waterproofing Stain & Sealer is the product to reach for when a fence has seen better days. Solid stain hides gray weathering, replacement boards, old stain blotches and the green tint of treated lumber, giving the whole fence one uniform color. On vertical surfaces, solid stains last longer than any semi-transparent product, and owners frequently report several years before a recoat is needed. It is an acrylic product sold and tinted at Home Depot, so colors are wide and touch-up cans are easy to find. It cleans up with soap and water. The tradeoffs are the ones that come with any film. It hides the grain completely, so it is a poor choice for a new cedar fence you want to show off. It can peel if applied over an old penetrating stain that still repels water or onto damp wood, so clean well and let the fence dry. Plan on two coats for even color. Prices were roughly 40 to 55 dollars per gallon at the time of writing."
